= 30×  magnification
20

InstrumentationOlympiad Handout
Switch to a 10mm, and you’re at 750/10 = 75×.
But magnification isn’t everything.  Eyepieces also have an apparent
field of view (AFOV), measured in degrees.  This is how wide the
view feels when you look into it.  Cheap eyepieces might have a
narrow 40°–50° AFOV, like looking through a tunnel.  Wide-field
eyepieces can go 70°, 82°, or even 100°, which feels more like a
window.  A wider field makes finding and tracking objects easier,
especially at high power.
