large declination adjustments and simplifying the measurement.
Procedure for FOV Measurement:
30

InstrumentationOlympiad Handout
1.Position the star at the eastern edge of the field, but on the midline.  Don’t just plop it anywhere,
move the telescope so the star is on the *eastern* side of the field, but exactly on the horizontal
line that runs through the center.
2.Wait for it to reach the center, then start the timer.  Let the star drift naturally toward the
center of the field.  The moment it crosses the exact center (the intersection of your crosshair),
that’s when you hit start on the stopwatch.
3.
Stop the timer when it reaches the western edge.  Keep tracking it with your eyes.  Don’t touch
the telescope.  The star will keep drifting west.  The moment it touches the *western* edge of
the field, hit stop.  That time (t
half
) is the time it took to travel across the *radius* of the field.
4.The time you just measured is for half the field (center to edge).  We need the full diameter time,
just multiply t
half
by 2.
t
